;CARE SHOULD BE EXERCISED IN INTERPRETING THE CURRENT MODEL,
DUE TO THE LIMITED (3.5 ANGSTROMS) RESOLUTION.  THE OVERALL
COORDINATE ERROR IS ESTIMATED TO BE APPROXIMATELY 0.45-0.60
ANGSTROMS, BUT THE ERROR IS HIGHER IN REGIONS HAVING HIGH
TEMPERATURE FACTORS.  PRECISE ASSIGNMENT OF HYDROGEN BONDS,
OTHER CONTACTS AND SECONDARY STRUCTURAL ELEMENTS AT THIS
RESOLUTION IS NOT POSSIBLE.  ATOMS WITH TEMPERATURE FACTORS
GREATER THAN 65 ANGSTROMS SQUARED SHOULD BE INTERPRETED
WITH CAUTION. RESIDUES 1-8 OF HA1 ARE NOT VISIBLE IN THE
ELECTRON DENSITY MAP.
;
